{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>El ha-kubbah.</b> Like <b>el ha-ohel</b> (to the tent). And likewise <b>qarov</b> in the language of Kedar, though there is a slight difference between the form of <b>ha-ohel</b> and <b>ha-kubbah</b>." "<b>Va-ydaq.</b> Like <b>u-dqarni</b> (and pierce me)." "<b>El kubbatah.</b> In the kubbah that was there with the brothers of Zimri. And some say that <b>kubbatah</b> is from the root of <b>ha-zero'a ve-ha-lechiyim ve-ha-qabbah</b> (the arm and the cheeks and the stomach). And there is also a way of midrash, that ten miracles were performed for Phinehas, only Scripture did not mention them."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra draws an analogy between the syntactic construction of אל הקבה and אל האהל; the reference to 'the language of Kedar' concerns Arabic cognates."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:29.395041246Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}